# Epistemic Recursion
## Second-Order Governance and the Closing of the Loop

**Outline v0.3** — Third of three. Assumes *Epistemic Governance for Agent Memory* v2.2 (L1) and *Epistemic Resolution* v0.3 (L2). Covers L3, L4, and L5.

*Changes in v0.3: the correspondence test moves from raw correlation to residual (§8); the frozen relational probe set is no longer this paper's mechanism, having been derived as a calibration requirement in the resolution paper (§7.1); the attenuation question is identified with an edge-level question in the governance paper (§3.2); execution fidelity transposes (§5.4). Changes in v0.2: new §6 on boundary accounting, which gives this paper ownership of a problem the governance paper withdrew; corrected discriminating experiment in §9, which as previously stated did not satisfy its own methodological requirement; second-order environmental drift added to §7; two experiments added.*

