The test belongs on the residual, not on the raw correlation. A binary high/low reading assumes the axes are either the same measurement or independent ones. There is a third case and it is probably the likeliest: two instruments accessing one underlying property while each remains sensitive to something the other is not. Raw correlation is then moderate, which the table above cannot interpret.
Regress the structural profile on the functional profile and test the residual for informativeness. L2's channel closes if the residual carries information about relations that the functional profile alone does not — not if the two profiles are uncorrelated.
Under that reading the resolution paper's two requirements stop conflicting. Locally, a genuine relation should register on both instruments, since a defect present in a claim pair should be visible from either access mode. Globally, the profiles must not reduce to one another. Co-detection plus an informative residual is exactly the signature of two access modes to one property, and it is what the architecture should be predicting rather than the stronger claim that the axes are independent.
The prediction still runs against the architecture, which is the right direction. A residual carrying no information is evidence that the second limb is not a limb.
Two consequences to state in advance so they read as predictions rather than accommodation. Fan-out is a structural quantity and appears among Reliability's indicators in the governance paper (§6.6) at low weight; under a two-axis result it should be dropped from that model rather than down-weighted, which is checkable against T1.2's residuals. And the granularity at which functional identity stabilises need not be the granularity at which structural identity does, in which case the architecture has two units of governance and needs a stated correspondence between them.
9. Emergence and the Discriminating Experiment
Emergence, if it occurs, occurs across passes rather than within one. The minimum measurable unit is two full navigations and the interesting quantity is second-order: whether improvement per pass is holding, growing, or decaying.
What the loop is for. Convergence of claim individuation by iteration — governance supplies a rough initial segmentation, resolution refines it, the second-order tier validates and generalises, L5 remits as evidence, repeat. Coherence improvement is the observable; individuation convergence is the mechanism. Measuring coherence without measuring individuation stability measures a symptom.
9.1 The discriminating experiment, corrected
The v0.1 design does not satisfy the methodological requirement the governance paper states, and the correction matters because this is the experiment the whole architecture rests on.
v0.1 compared N passes over evidence set E against one pass over N×E. Those two conditions differ in total evidence, final store size, query distribution, and total compute simultaneously. It is a comparison across environments, which measures environments. Any difference is attributable to at least four uncontrolled variables.
Corrected design. Hold total evidence fixed at E and total compute fixed at C across both arms. Vary only the number of loop closures.
Arm R: N passes over E, compute budget C.
Arm S: one pass over E, compute budget C, with the additional compute spent on within-pass iteration — more comparisons, deeper propagation, more thorough adjudication.
Both arms end with the same evidence and have consumed the same compute. The only difference is whether the tier boundaries were crossed N times or once.
That isolates the quantity of interest, which was never "more processing helps" but "closure helps." If Arm R outperforms Arm S at matched evidence and matched compute, something is produced by traversing the loop that is not produced by doing more work inside it. That is the recursion signature and nothing else in the architecture predicts it.
Both arms are evaluated against the frozen relational probe set (§7.1), not against their own live streams.
9.2 The failure it must be distinguished from
A loop transmitting vigorously where both poles already generate what crosses. The signature is not improvement without new evidence — genuine reorganisation of a fixed corpus should produce some — but improvement without new evidence that never saturates. A fixed-point iteration approaches a limit; self-agreement does not. Saturation is therefore the predicted behaviour and its absence is the alarm, which inverts the naive reading.
9.3 Proof-of-concept target
One marginal but measurable improvement in coherence after a full navigation, with all three closure conditions met.
Candidate measure: the register of unreconciled contradictions, paired against detection rate — a system that resolves contradictions by failing to detect them scores perfectly on the unpaired version. Resolutions must also be attributed by limb, since a register that drains entirely through first-order demotion demonstrates that the governance paper works, which was not in question. Only resolutions attributable to L3 — a relational description showing two claims were never in conflict — are evidence the closure does anything.
9.4 Two further experiments
Parallelism is a third condition, not a neutral one. L3 and L4 run in parallel by design, and the paper assumes this is equivalent to either serial order minus the waiting. That is untested. Run three arms — L3 then L4, L4 then L3, and parallel — on matched stores. If the parallel arm differs from both serial arms, the arrangement has effects of its own and §4.3's waste analysis is incomplete.
Replication. Re-run the validated configuration on a store of different provenance and domain with no re-tuning, and compare the improvement-per-pass profile rather than the endpoint. A profile that replicates indicates an architecture; one requiring re-tuning indicates a configuration fitted to one store. This is the second-order form of the governance paper's T3.4 and it is the single strongest external check available.
10. Open Problems
Where the tier structure stops. If transposition is genuine, third-order relations are available. Nothing here argues two is principled rather than convenient.
Whether analogy is a coordinate (§4.4). Determines whether L4 is boundable.
Attenuation (§3.2). Whether mediated external constraint is external constraint, and whether the narrow channel supports the tier.
What a counterexample to a relation is (§2.2). Determines whether the terminal path exists at second order.
The baseline problem (§7.1). Compounding across passes, and worse here than in either predecessor.
Cost. Second-order operations are pairwise over relations, which are themselves pairwise over claims. Naively quartic. The resolution paper has no triage function and this paper needs one more urgently.
Whether coherence and individuation-convergence can be measured independently. §9 asserts one is observable and the other is mechanism. If the only available measure of individuation convergence is coherence, the distinction is not operational and §9.3's target is circular.
Whether the architecture ever needs the exchange rate (§6.3). Boundary accounting locates the missing conversion without supplying it. If some decision requires comparing governance compute to protected capacity directly, the gap becomes blocking rather than merely visible.
11. Notes on Drafting
Lead with §3.3. L1 cannot ground its own edges and L3 can. That is the argument for the tier existing, it closes a stated hole in the governance paper, and it is concrete in a way the emergence claims are not. Introduce the recursion as what makes it possible rather than as the headline.
§6 is the second deliverable and should be positioned as one. Boundary accounting resolves a problem the governance paper explicitly withdrew, and it does so structurally rather than by supplying a number. Two concrete resolutions to stated first-order gaps is a stronger case for the paper than any claim about emergence.
Keep §3.2 in the first section. The attenuation risk is the paper's largest and burying it in open problems would be the move the predecessors have been careful not to make.
§9.1's correction should be visible, not silent. The original design failed a requirement the companion paper states, and saying so is worth more than quietly shipping the better version — it demonstrates the requirement has teeth.
The paper is short. Most machinery is inherited; the content is transfer conditions, boundary accounting, and the two places transposition fails. If it comes out as long as either predecessor, something has been re-derived that should have been cited.